{"title":"2024 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Narsa buys a package of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Monday morning. The bar graph shows the number of cookies that Narsa eats each day from Monday to Friday.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>How many cookies are left in the package after Friday?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cbaabea58ee75b816f59b2683b261b8c7f4bcf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 45 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 25 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can subtract the total number of cookies that Narsa ate from the number of cookies that the package had.\n</p><p>From the bar graph, we can see that Narsa ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Monday, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Tuesday, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Wednesday, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Thursday, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cookies on Friday. \n</p><p>In total, Narsa ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2093aca1572b731abb87c2a5cd00d7b6b29575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 12 + 8 + 0 + 6 = 16 + 8 + 6 = 24 + 6 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"366\" height=\"15\" /> cookies.\n</p><p>Since the package originally had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cookies, this means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed695cc16ef106971ac595c18b620925d809d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 - 30 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"150\" height=\"30\" /> cookies remaining.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"backgroun